hen stir in the starch slurry and cook for 2–3 minutes until a glossy pourable gravy forms.","Return paneer and toss gently for 1–2 minutes. Finish with spring onion and serve immediately; taste before adding salt because the sauces already contain it."],"tips":["Cook one test piece first to check seasoning, binding and cooking temperature before finishing the batch."],"substitutions":[],"status":"complete","prepTime":35,"passiveTime":null,"notes":"Quantities are for four adult portions. Cooking times are estimates; use the doneness checks in each step. Ingredient costs use sample rates and exclude unpriced items.","photo":{"name":"Chilli Paneer Gravy","src":"/photos/chilli-paneer-gravy-1200.webp","small":"/photos/chilli-paneer-gravy-600.webp","width":1200,"height":900,"alt":"Chilli Paneer Gravy served ready to eat","kind":"generated","title":"Chilli Paneer Gravy","author":"OpenAI image generation","changes":"AI-generated serving illustration, resized and converted to WebP.","status":"reviewed","sourceWidth":1448,"sourceHeight":1086,"reviewedAt":"2026-09-18"}}'::jsonb,true) on conflict(dish_id) do update set recipe=excluded.recipe,published=true;
insert into public.kkk_recipes(dish_id,recipe,published) values('veg-manchurian-dry','{"id":"veg-manchurian-dry","name":"Veg Manchurian Dry","baseServings":4,"batchSize":20,"ingredients":[{"name":"cabbage","qty":350,"unit":"g","group":"Other","scale":"linear"},{"name":"carrot","qty":180,"unit":"g","group":"Vegetables","scale":"linear","pricePerUnit":0.06},{"name":"capsicum","qty":100,"unit":"g","group":"Vegetables","scale":"linear"},{"name":"plain flour","qty":80,"unit":"g","group":"Grains","scale":"linear"},{"name":"cornflour starch","qty":60,"unit":"g","group":"Grains","scale":"linear"},{"name":"ginger","qty":15,"unit":"g","group":"Other","scale":"linear"},{"name":"garlic","qty":18,"unit":"g","group":"Other","scale":"linear"},{"name":"soy sauce","qty":35,"unit":"ml","group":"Other","scale":"linear"},{"name":"tomato ketchup","qty":40,"unit":"g","group":"Vegetables","scale":"linear"},{"name":"chilli sauce","qty":25,"unit":"g","group":"Spices","scale":"seasoning","pricePerUnit":0.65},{"name":"rice vinegar","qty":20,"unit":"ml","group":"Grains","scale":"linear"},{"name":"spring onion","qty":80,"unit":"g","group":"Vegetables","scale":"linear"},{"name":"salt","qty":3,"unit":"g","group":"Spices","scale":"seasoning","pricePerUnit":0.025},{"name":"oil","qty":20,"unit":"ml","group":"Packaged","scale":"linear","pricePerUnit":0.15},{"name":"oil for frying","qty":600,"unit":"ml","group":"Packaged","scale":"linear"},{"name":"water","qty":180,"unit":"ml","group":"Other","scale":"linear","pricePerUnit":0}],"steps":["Finely shred cabbage and carrot and mince capsicum. Mix with plain flour, 40 g starch, half the ginger and garlic, and salt; the vegetables should release enough moisture to bind. Add water only a teaspoon at a time if dry.","Shape 16 small balls firmly. Heat frying oil to about 170°C in a deep pan less than half full and fry one test ball; add a little flour if it breaks.","Fry the remaining balls in batches for 4–5 minutes until golden and cooked through, then drain.","Heat 20 ml oil, stir-fry remaining ginger and garlic with spring onion whites for 30 seconds. Add soy sauce, ketchup, chilli sauce, vinegar and all but 60 ml measured water.","Mix remaining starch with the reserved cold water. Stir into the simmering sauce and cook for 2–3 minutes until glossy and thickened.","Add fried balls only at serving time and toss gently. Finish with spring onion greens; keep sauce separate if preparing ahead to preserve texture."],"tips":["Frying oil is a working quantity and is not all absorbed."],"substitutions":[],"status":"complete","prepTime":50,"passiveTime":null,"notes":"Quantities are for four adult portions. Cooking times are estimates; use the doneness checks in each step. Ingredient costs use sample rates and exclude unpriced items.","photo":{"name":"Veg Manchurian Dry","src":"/photos/veg-manchurian-dry-1200.webp","small":"/photos/veg-manchurian-dry-600.webp","width":1200,"height":900,"alt":"Veg Manchurian Dry served ready to eat","kind":"generated","title":"Veg Manchurian Dry","author":"OpenAI image generation","changes":"AI-generated photorealistic recipe photograph, resized and converted to WebP.","status":"reviewed","sourceWidth":1448,"sourceHeight":1086,"reviewedAt":"2026-09-27"}}'::jsonb,true) on conflict(dish_id) do update set recipe=excluded.recipe,published=true;
